sing: Phones can process data, but cloud models might not have the same processing power or data storage.\n7", "outputSample": "<think>\nOkay, the user wants me to list 25 distinct things that on-device AI can do a phone do a cloud model can't, each with two full sentences of explanation. They mentioned that the numbered blocks", "provenance": {"definitions": "prefill tok/s = prompt_tokens / (prompt_eval_end_ms - inference_start_ms) * 1000. The window opens before the runner tokenizes the prompt (TextLLMRunner::generate sets inference_start_ms, then encodes), so prefill includes tokenization.\nTTFT ms = first_token_ms - inference_start_ms = the same window (first_token_ms is taken when prefill returns, before the first token is decoded to text).\ndecode tok/s = generated_tokens / (inference_end_ms - prompt_eval_end_ms) * 1000, generated_tokens = tokens of the decode loop; the reply has one more token, the one prefill sampled.\ncold = one generation in a fresh llama_main process (no --warmup). warm = llama_main --warmup: one unmeasured generation of the same prompt and max_new_tokens in the same process, stats and KV position reset, the second generation measured.\nClock: integer milliseconds (extension/llm/runner/util.h time_in_ms).", "recipe": "Qwen3-0.6B-ET1.5.1-mlx-4w-emb8-ctx2048.recipe.json", "recipeSha256": "25bd2ecb3f9417e03f61e94e319afc1fda64385f976936ce229028e768596702", "recipeAlias": "et1.5.1-mlx-4w-g128-emb8", "exporter": "extension/llm/export/export_llm (examples/models/qwen3/config/qwen3_xnnpack_q8da4w.yaml)", "modelProvenance": "own export with the ExecuTorch tag's own exporter (recipe.json beside the .pte); not a published artifact", "promptFile": "Qwen3-0.6B-ET1.5.1-mlx-4w-emb8-ctx2048.prompts/long-context-1024-gen256.chat.txt", "promptSha256": "e8cfb3f021c4ce7c00b3ea24d91950ad3f5dd8f64dceb58a5058be68539b0fd9", "tokenizer": "tokenizer.json", "tokenizerSha256": "aeb13307a71acd8fe81861d94ad54ab689df773318809eed3cbe794b4492dae4", "textExtraction": "std